From 1e1a981fe9a0e70dbdd57f00047261569b56451f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:10:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Render and sample the Liquid Glass attachment formats

macOS 26 and 27 draw their Setup Assistant panels through RG16Uint
targets that a later pass samples, beside a memoryless RG32Float colour
attachment. Neither was renderable, so every panel pass was refused and
the panels never appeared.

Both become texel layouts: rendered and sampled natively as R16G16_UINT
and R32G32_SFLOAT, resident at their own format. An integer layout needs
COLOR_ATTACHMENT only, since it never blends. The CPU seed, readback and
Store converters get lossy arms so the renderable-set invariant holds;
the resident rail is what keeps them exact. The capability word gives the
image dimension 24 bits to make room for the two new layout bits.

27.2 now draws its language panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
